    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **61 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived, read-only `selfLink` field to the Owner representation, equal to `/api/owners/` followed by the owner's id.\n\nSince the `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated by MapStruct, two edits were needed:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so it's part of the generated DTO and API docs.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that derives `selfLink` as `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()`, alongside the other derived fields (displayName, salutation, etc.).\n\nBecause the mapper feeds both `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (POST response) and `RespondWithOwner` (GET response), `selfLink` now appears on both. The new `Cp49Tests` (which creates an owner then reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `$.selfLink == /api/owners/{id}`) passes, and all 61 existing tests still pass.",
